BakaSU: drop the stray return from the manual-hook preinit stub

BakaSU 516d3e87 defines ksu_preinit_handle_execve_manual() as a void
function but returns false.  clang 22 (r596125) makes -Wreturn-mismatch a
default error, so drivers/kernelsu/core/init.o fails to build.  The
function is an empty stub under CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK; drop the return
instead of pointing the submodule at a local commit.

Same fix as kernel/oneplus/sdm845/patches/bakasu-preinit.patch.

Apply this after updating the KernelSU submodule.

From the kernel tree root:

    git -C KernelSU apply "$(pwd)/patches/bakasu-preinit.patch"

Or from inside the KernelSU submodule:

    git apply ../patches/bakasu-preinit.patch

diff --git a/kernel/preinit/preinit.h b/kernel/preinit/preinit.h
index 9e49bcd8..1ba59075 100644
--- a/kernel/preinit/preinit.h
+++ b/kernel/preinit/preinit.h
@@ -47,7 +47,6 @@ static inline bool ksu_preinit_handle_execve_tracepoint(const char __user **file
 #elif defined(CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK)
 static inline void ksu_preinit_handle_execve_manual(const char **filename, struct user_arg_ptr *argv)
 {
-    return false;
 }
 #elif defined(CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS)
 static inline int ksu_setup_preinit_file(struct filename **filename_ptr, struct user_arg_ptr *argv_user)
